ed":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T20:16:16-07:00","id":466917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466898#post466898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh... In my opinion, WoD is too empowering to humanity to play well with the Lovecraft mythos. Lovecraft's stories were all about how small and insignificant humans are in the face of omnipotent uncaring gods from the farthest reaches of the cosmos. In the World of Darkness, every single human has the potential within their soul to become a living symbol that can define and re-define reality any way it sees fit, and artificial beings wielding the divine fire would gladly give up their power to become human... I just don't see them meshing well, at least not without damaging a big part of what makes the Lovecraft mythos so horrifying. That said, there are plenty of godlike alien beings in WoD, so it should theoretically be possible if you aren't married to Lovecraft's themes of existential nihilism. Wouldn't be my choice, but different strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd check out the various stories featuring Randolph Carter! He's something way more then any human could be, I'd write him either has a Changeling or Mage (maybe transitioning between the two in his adventures), I don't know enough about either line to actually place him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T21:01:10-07:00","id":466974,"title":"","content":"He's Yog Sothoth at a specific point in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T21:42:16-07:00","id":466994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466847#post466847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Triage might qualify, He's rank 6, he's in the GMC, and he time travels around like nbd.<br /> <br /> He also might be a machine snake body with a lionhead, I don't recall exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are his servants, the Blind Serpents. Triage himself is a lion with a metal mane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:59:23-07:00","id":467113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466909#post466909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think his protagonist were just a bunch of pussies.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>That particular sort of language is unwelcome here. Please don't use it.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T01:17:05-07:00","id":467117,"title":"","content":"Considering the rather relevant current time where Bloodborne has been a popular piece of media with a heavy Lovecraft influence people need to always remember two things if nothing else when inserting one media, genre convention, whatever into another setting.<br /> <br /> 1. You never should expect to insert it whole cloth. The whole point is that they are two separate medias you are going to combine. Blending is part of the process. In this case it means don't latch onto any one piece of the nature of Lovecraft's work and declare how it means it doesn't work. Adding media to a setting really doesn't work that way organically if you still want a compelling setting.<br /> <br /> 2. Remember not to confuse derivative media with the original. A lot of the Mythos stuff people latch onto isn't Lovecraft but stuff like Chaosium,etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T02:31:18-07:00","id":467135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466974#post466974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's Yog Sothoth at a specific point in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to elaborate please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:19:23-07:00","id":467274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467113#post467113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>That particular sort of language is unwelcome here. Please don't use it.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mah bad. I typed &quot;wussies&quot; and my damn phone autocorrected it. Rest assured, the proper term has been added to the dictionary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:38:34-07:00","id":467310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodspeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467135#post467135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to elaborate please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Randolph Carter is an avatar of Yog-Sothoth. You know that whole &quot;we're all aspects of the Universal mind separated from the whole so that It can experience Itself&quot; deal you find in Eastern religion and New Age thought? Basically that. Except that it appears that only SOME beings are rather than all.<br /> <br /> Presumably that would make everything else a parasite.<br /> <br /> Anyway... Azathoth is a good candidate for the God-Machine and Yog-Sothoth seems kinda Principle-like. Shub-Niggurath is an Old God who used to rule over the Primal Wild and is now one of the Bound. Cthulhu is, as I noted previously, a Beast (Makara/Ruin) whose human form is one of the &quot;deathless Chinamen&quot; who runs the cult from the plateau of Leng. Probably he has really epic facial hair that looks like tentacles or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:39:17-07:00","id":467376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467117#post467117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the rather relevant current time where Bloodborne has been a popular piece of media with a heavy Lovecraft influence people need to always remember two things if nothing else when inserting one media, genre convention, whatever into another setting.<br /> <br /> 1. You never should expect to insert it whole cloth. The whole point is that they are two separate medias you are going to combine. Blending is part of the process. In this case it means don't latch onto any one piece of the nature of Lovecraft's work and declare how it means it doesn't work. Adding media to a setting really doesn't work that way organically if you still want a compelling setting.<br /> <br /> 2. Remember not to confuse derivative media with the original. A lot of the Mythos stuff people latch onto isn't Lovecraft but stuff like Chaosium,etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and apologies if I came off wrongheaded; I did not mean to suggest that Lovecraft-inspired works all need to contain existential horror. It's just that I personally dislike when that theme is not included in Lovecraft-derivative works because it's one of my favorite aspects of the original, and wanted to share why I felt that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:49:57-07:00","id":467386,"title":"","content":"I know exactly how you feel, Charlaquin.<br /> <br /> But I want to point out that there's supposed to be a lot more to the World of Darkness than is limited to the books we have on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:05:47-07:00","id":467441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467310#post467310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Randolph Carter is an avatar of Yog-Sothoth. You know that whole &quot;we're all aspects of the Universal mind separated from the whole so that It can experience Itself&quot; deal you find in Eastern religion and New Age thought? Basically that. Except that it appears that only SOME beings are rather than all.<br /> <br /> Presumably that would make everything else a parasite.<br /> <br /> Anyway... Azathoth is a good candidate for the God-Machine and Yog-Sothoth seems kinda Principle-like. Shub-Niggurath is an Old God who used to rule over the Primal Wild and is now one of the Bound. Cthulhu is, as I noted previously, a Beast (Makara/Ruin) whose human form is one of the &quot;deathless Chinamen&quot; who runs the cult from the plateau of Leng. Probably he has really epic facial hair that looks like tentacles or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I am familiar with the concept but my question was more along the lines of, &quot;where is this written&quot;? If this is your personal interpretation and/or theory that's cool too, I just want to know which is which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:52:40-07:00","id":467536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467376#post467376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true, and apologies if I came off wrongheaded; I did not mean to suggest that Lovecraft-inspired works all need to contain existential horror. It's just that I personally dislike when that theme is not included in Lovecraft-derivative works because it's one of my favorite aspects of the original, and wanted to share why I felt that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did not come across as wrongheaded. I just was reminded of some things when I was thinking on a recent Exalted Ask Dev's discussion on why Jeet Kune Do does not work whole cloth trying to insert it into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:21:21-07:00","id":467557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodspeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467441#post467441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes I am familiar with the concept but my question was more along the lines of, &amp;quot;where is this written&amp;quot;? If this is your personal interpretation and/or theory that's cool too, I just want to know which is which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Through the Gates of the Silver Key, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:44:25-07:00","id":467577,"title":"","content":"Can we get a clarification on how wide the net of &quot;Lovecraft mythos&quot; we're tossing is? Or, at least, what the OP is looking for?<br /> <br /> Are we considering stuff like <a href=\"http://mockman.com/2011/03/21/celephais-page-1/\" target=\"_blank\">Celephais</a>, which consists entirely of one man's search for the city of his youth through opiates?<br /> <br /> The core of Lovecraft was his disdain for modernity, a pining for tradition, and his distaste for the teeming masses of humanity. I think the NWoD likes humanity a bit too much to mesh well with Lovecraft's themes.<br /> <br /> After all, if all you want to do is wedge the Old Ones and the Elder Gods into the WoD... Well, Nyarlathothep is an Angel, or a collection of Angels, if you don't feel comfortable with giving one Angel &quot;a thousand&quot; forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:44:54-07:00","id":467578,"title":"","content":"I've honestly been trying to tap Lovecraftian themes in Mage recently, and a couple of things that came to me are the notion of Really Big Things that could dwell just about anywhere - the Astral, the Shadow, out in space, in some other nebulous half-realm, etc. - whose natures can be roughly be mapped to motives (so, for example, a being whose nature is aligned with consumption might be said to want to devour things, even though such is not an active want; it consumes because it is its nature to consume, just as it is gravity's nature to attract). These things might be sources of a kind of Magical Tradition; using their symbols as a means of enacting great power in the physical world without needing to worry about messy Abyssal troubles.<br /> <br /> I've also had thoughts for a Beast-Mage crossover, tapping into the Primordial Dream's effects on the minds of humans and using their &quot;natural rituals&quot; that result as a kind of metaphysical hunting hound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:49:44-07:00","id":467694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467577#post467577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get a clarification on how wide the net of &amp;quot;Lovecraft mythos&amp;quot; we're tossing is? Or, at least, what the OP is looking for?<br /> <br /> Are we considering stuff like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://mockman.com/2011/03/21/celephais-page-1/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Celephais</a>, which consists entirely of one man's search for the city of his youth through opiates?<br /> <br /> The core of Lovecraft was his disdain for modernity, a pining for tradition, and his distaste for the teeming masses of humanity. I think the NWoD likes humanity a bit too much to mesh well with Lovecraft's themes.<br /> <br /> After all, if all you want to do is wedge the Old Ones and the Elder Gods into the WoD... Well, Nyarlathothep is an Angel, or a collection of Angels, if you don't feel comfortable with giving one Angel &amp;quot;a thousand&amp;quot; forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, &quot;Lovecraft's cosmic horror stories and Dreamlands stuff are nonfiction in the WoD, though the usual caveats about unreliable narrators apply.&quot;<br /> <br /> And as I pointed out above, the themes may be the result of his protagonists being mostly a bunch of wussies. Considering the fact that his most notable third-person tales (The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath, The Dunwich Horror, and The Case of Charles Dexter Ward) end with the monsters vanquished and humanity triumphant (at least for today), Lovecraft's own corpus supports this interpretation.<br /> <br /> In other words, Lovecraft's fiction isn't about the player characters. It's about the cannon fodder NPCs whose strange death/disappearance/madness acts as a plot hook to get the PCs involved and kicking ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:49:53-07:00","id":467695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=467557#post467557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Through the Gates of the Silver Key, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I think I remember now but I will check it again because it seems I wasn't paying enough attention when I read it the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:43:36-07:00","id":473593,"title":"","content":"Ok so how about some of the weird super-science/magic cults/corps from CthulhuTech in the nWoD? Like the Tagers of the Eldritch Society or maybe the Dhohanoids of the Crysalis Corporation ... though the Engels might be truly horrifying in a God Machine game as the GM experiments with manifested Angels to that came be used in the open to stop the Unchained...ooohh ideas ideas ideas ..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:55:30-07:00","id":473604,"title":"","content":"I think I recall someone trying to homebrew the Tagers into a Hunter the Vigil conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:29:02-07:00","id":473838,"title":"","content":"Having listened to the rock opera adaptation of Dreams in the Witch-House (yes, that's a thing, and it's amazeballs) on repeat for the last few days, I have decided that Azathoth has to be an Abyssal Watchtower.<br /> <br /> I mean, Gilman has crazy-ass dreams that spill over into reality (mystery play) culminating in a visit to a terrifying realm where he signs his name in a book (Awakening). And while Azathoth's court might bear some superficial resemblance to Pandemonium, it's most certainly not in the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T23:34:30-07:00","id":473930,"title":"","content":"Conflicting themes aside, it is possible to convert characters from the Mythos into similar NWOD versions, due to the sheer variety of supernatural beings that exist in the latter. You could go the easy route and just make them all Aliens (Mage: The Awakening - Summoners, Chapter Four).<br /> <br /> So, here are some suggestions, as imagined by other users and by myself. I am including works related to/inspired by the Mythos. If you don't agree with these interpretations and think others might be better, please let me know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cthulhu = Makara Beast<br /> <br /> Nyarlathotep = God-Machine Angel or Principle Angel<br /> <br /> Yog-Sothoth = Astral Archetype of Infinity, most certainly Rank 6 or more<br /> <br /> Shub-Niggurath = Supernal Beast (Atavism) or maybe True Fae <br /> <br /> Azatoth = Abyssal<br /> <br /> Hastur = True Fae<br /> <br /> Byakhee, Mi-Go, Elder Things, Hounds of Tindalos, Yithians, Ghouls and other, less vast monsters = Cryptids, Hobgoblins or Aliens<br /> <br /> Titus Crow = Hunter (that reminds me, we really need a British Compact or Conspiracy)<br /> <br /> Randolph Carter = Changeling (Darkling) or Mage (Mastigos)<br /> <br /> Conan = Mage (Thyrsus)<br /> <br /> Herbert West = Genius <br /> <br /> Elder Gods, such as Nodens and Bast = True Fae or Spirits with high Rank<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T23:37:54-07:00","id":473932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=473838#post473838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Gilman has crazy-ass dreams that spill over into reality (mystery play) culminating in a visit to a terrifying realm where he signs his name in a book (Awakening). And while Azathoth's court might bear some superficial resemblance to Pandemonium, it's most certainly not in the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where not Yog-Sothoth being mentioned by Angerboda ( iconic Scelasti chracter ) in <b>Inferno</b>'s <b>Mage</b> Section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T00:03:32-07:00","id":473944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=473932#post473932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where not Yog-Sothoth being mentioned by Angerboda ( iconic Scelasti chracter ) in <b>Inferno</b>'s <b>Mage</b> Section?</div> </div> </div> </div>Angrboda laughs when he quotes Lovecraft, and Morvran testily dismisses him and says Lovecraft doesn't scare him. Angrboda is taunting his captor by joking around and referring to mass-market paperback characters when he's talking about the Abyss, rather than any of the names he actually knows gulmoth by. That's why Morvran is annoyed and doesn't ask what the hell Angrboda means by that; he knows exactly what Angrboda means, Angrboda means &quot;just because you have me chained up doesn't mean I'm intimidated enough to take you seriously.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of that is irrelevant to this thread, of course.<br /> <br /> I quite like the idea of Azathoth serving the role of an Abyssal Watchtower as well as some other roles, likely sort of budding off constituent entities like the other great Annunaki; Abyssal entities blur the line between people, places, objects, events and concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T00:57:38-07:00","id":473974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=473944#post473944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Angrboda laughs when he quotes Lovecraft, and Morvran testily dismisses him and says Lovecraft doesn't scare him. Angrboda is taunting his captor by joking around and referring to mass-market paperback characters when he's talking about the Abyss, rather than any of the names he actually knows gulmoth by. That's why Morvran is annoyed and doesn't ask what the hell Angrboda means by that; he knows exactly what Angrboda means, Angrboda means &quot;just because you have me chained up doesn't mean I'm intimidated enough to take you seriously.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of that is irrelevant to this thread, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277130-abyss-and-cthulhu-mythos?p=277183#post277183\">And retreading old conversational ground besides.</a><br /> <br /> I do wonder how much of the Mythos fits into Abyssal metaphysics versus, say, the Depths or the merely Phenomenal, particularly given the level of commonality that a lot of supernatural entities approach with godlike power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:39:31-07:00","id":474717,"title":"","content":"Re: Attempts to classify the various Lovecraftian beasties into various niches, my sincerest recommendation is &quot;Do not do this&quot;. A big part of this kind of horror is a complete dearth of means to classify these things. They simply <i>are</i>, and the moment you can realize that, hey, Hastur can be defeated with cold iron or Shub-Niggurath is from the Primal Wild, you suddenly understand these things and can effectively oppose them.<br /> <br /> A part of the horror of Lovecraftian works is that, in the rare event you can ever oppose these things, the most you can do is slay some meaningless minions. The thing itself is unknowable, untouchable, and utterly beyond you.<br /> <br /> If you can say what Yog-Sothoth can and cannot do with any degree of certainty, it is no longer Yog-Sothoth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:00:10-07:00","id":474761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=474717#post474717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Attempts to classify the various Lovecraftian beasties into various niches, my sincerest recommendation is &quot;Do not do this&quot;. A big part of this kind of horror is a complete dearth of means to classify these things. They simply <i>are</i>, and the moment you can realize that, hey, Hastur can be defeated with cold iron or Shub-Niggurath is from the Primal Wild, you suddenly understand these things and can effectively oppose them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold iron doesn't really have much bearing on &quot;does it want to tap us for delicious CSF or does it want to wear our skin and have intimate relations with our various loved ones or is it a part of the defining fundament of reality or is it just a Weird Thing That Simply Exists.&quot; That's not so much &quot;niche&quot; as it is &quot;animal, vegetable, mineral.&quot;<br /> <br /> Having a decent guess at whether or not the weird aliens are going to unmake all of coherent existence with their presence is not quite on the level of having a formal classification of any exterminatorial use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:26:40-07:00","id":474836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=474717#post474717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Attempts to classify the various Lovecraftian beasties into various niches, my sincerest recommendation is &amp;quot;Do not do this&amp;quot;. A big part of this kind of horror is a complete dearth of means to classify these things. They simply <i>are</i>, and the moment you can realize that, hey, Hastur can be defeated with cold iron or Shub-Niggurath is from the Primal Wild, you suddenly understand these things and can effectively oppose them.<br /> <br /> A part of the horror of Lovecraftian works is that, in the rare event you can ever oppose these things, the most you can do is slay some meaningless minions. The thing itself is unknowable, untouchable, and utterly beyond you.<br /> <br /> If you can say what Yog-Sothoth can and cannot do with any degree of certainty, it is no longer Yog-Sothoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> The NWoD has things that are every bit as ineffable as any Lovecraftian creation. Annunaki, Elder Gods, True Fae, the Exarchs, the Principle and the God-Machine; none of them have stats. They are plot devices/setting elements, and if they take notice of you, &quot;slow painful death while gibbering incoherently&quot; is not the least pleasant of all possible outcomes.<br /> <br /> Then you have things like Leviathan from Book of the Dead that can't be killed (hence no stat block) but can be fought off temporarily (so Leviathan's tentacles have physical stats.)<br /> <br /> Remember, ramming a steamboat through Cthulhu's head is at least a temporary setback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:02:16-07:00","id":475139,"title":"","content":"Wierdly enough the Brineborn from Werewolf remind me of the Deep Ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:32:24-07:00","id":475182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475139#post475139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wierdly enough the Brineborn from Werewolf remind me of the Deep Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>What can you tell me of the Brineborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T20:14:48-07:00","id":475287,"title":"","content":"They're a piscine race of shapeshifters from the War Against The Pure splatbook. Basically deep one expies, their lore is that they are the children of a sea deity's emissary who tried and failed to bring civilisation to the land-dwelling humans, and so they are cursed. They need to be around water to be comfortable, but too long in the water and they start to drown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T20:28:25-07:00","id":475303,"title":"","content":"Yeah, despite being somewhat creepy fish-men, they're kind-of pathetic. Not saying that they can't be dangerous or competent; just that you can't help pitying them anymore than you can a dog with only two or three legs. I mean, they're Fishmen who have panic attacks if they swim too far out from the beach! It's telling that their culture is highly religious(both animists and more mainstream faiths) because their lives just suck that badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T21:00:18-07:00","id":475341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475303#post475303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, despite being somewhat creepy fish-men, they're kind-of pathetic. Not saying that they can't be dangerous or competent; just that you can't help pitying them anymore than you can a dog with only two or three legs. I mean, they're Fishmen who have panic attacks if they swim too far out from the beach! It's telling that their culture is highly religious(both animists and more mainstream faiths) because their lives just suck that badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Carl is the best fishman. This cannot be said enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T00:49:22-07:00","id":475499,"title":"","content":"The Uratha themselves always reminded me of the Deep Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T04:56:51-07:00","id":475635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475341#post475341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Carl is the best fishman. This cannot be said enough.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, that goes without saying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:38:44-07:00","id":475857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475341#post475341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Carl is the best fishman. This cannot be said enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is this Carl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:09:06-07:00","id":475916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475857#post475857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is this Carl?</div> </div> </div> </div> An example Brineborn given in War Against the Pure. Not the brightest candle in the menorah, but he comes off as a decent fellow, and a possible ally to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:12:32-07:00","id":475921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475857#post475857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is this Carl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sample Brineborn from <i>War Against the Pure</i>, whose combination of character traits happens to include &quot;fishman for Jesus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something's been committing gruesome murders in a little town at the north end of Jersey Shore and he's investigating because one of the victims was a boy he played with once at the arcade.<br /> <br /> Also werewolves may or may not have killed his pack-equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T15:18:31-07:00","id":476340,"title":"","content":"I think the Abyss and Astral Space make for a nice way of having the mythos come up in a game. The Temenos comprises the collective human unconsciousness, and everything thought of by humanity. A mythos thought of by an author would have its place within this great realm. But what if there is more to the Lovecraft's fiction than meets the eye? What if his conceptions of Cthulhu and the other Great Old Ones are manifestations of something true, or so blatantly untrue that their Lie manifests a mark in this world. This could very well be a piece of the Abyss, perhaps even the primordial history of the anti timeline told in the story of the Prince of 100,000 leaves. Or these old gods could have dwelled in the supernal realms, cast down by the Exarchs and bound to the fallen world. These Bound are dead, dreaming in transcendental spaces, unable to be truly destroyed or erased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T17:00:43-07:00","id":476429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=475921#post475921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sample Brineborn from <i>War Against the Pure</i>, whose combination of character traits happens to include &quot;fishman for Jesus.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always eerie when the strange races take up variants of mortal religion. The beshilu in Shadows of the UK have some sort of strange religious bent to them with a Messianic figure and everything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T11:08:09-07:00","id":603958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=476429#post476429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's always eerie when the strange races take up variants of mortal religion. The beshilu in Shadows of the UK have some sort of strange religious bent to them with a Messianic figure and everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it's probably just me projecting my biases, but I'd say that this is eerie because people who are religious or have religious close friends are rubbed the wrong way when they read stories about inhuman beings practicing filthy rituals and reciting dark litanies. Perhaps they see something of themselves in these mockeries? Like staring into a muddy, cracked mirror. There is enough similarity to give you pause and make you wonder, but it is different enough from what you accept as wholesome and natural that it is simply <i>unnerving. </i><br /> <br /> What could we call this? There's already the fitting &quot;Uncanny Valley&quot;, but what about &quot;Uncanny Flattery&quot;?<br /> <br /> ...I need to find time and inspiration to write up a One Shot Story Seed of religious horror and conflicting ideologies called &quot;Uncanny Flattery&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-26-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:58:00-07:00","id":604129,"title":"","content":"I think the God Machine is an obvious choice for simularities. It has in common with the Mythos that the GM doesn't <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">care about humanity at all except as tools, resources or hindrances in his plans. Their is no official explanation of what the God Machine really is and what it wants, so that's easy to give it a Cthulhu spin. Of course the GMC also have things in common with Kult and Dark City, namely the secret machinations behind the facade of the everyday world. So it isn't a 100% match, but it's close enough. Other game also have supreme beings, but those are specifically tied to certain lore.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T05:01:51-07:00","id":604599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466909#post466909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think his protagonists were just a bunch of wussbags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr Armitage kicked the Dunwich Horror's ass pretty hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T05:09:34-07:00","id":604603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=604599#post604599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dr Armitage kicked the Dunwich Horror's ass pretty hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Mate Johanssen of the Emma was pretty gutsy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:44:19-07:00","id":611456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=474717#post474717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Attempts to classify the various Lovecraftian beasties into various niches, my sincerest recommendation is &quot;Do not do this&quot;. A big part of this kind of horror is a complete dearth of means to classify these things. They simply <i>are</i>, and the moment you can realize that, hey, Hastur can be defeated with cold iron or Shub-Niggurath is from the Primal Wild, you suddenly understand these things and can effectively oppose them.<br /> <br /> A part of the horror of Lovecraftian works is that, in the rare event you can ever oppose these things, the most you can do is slay some meaningless minions. The thing itself is unknowable, untouchable, and utterly beyond you.<br /> <br /> If you can say what Yog-Sothoth can and cannot do with any degree of certainty, it is no longer Yog-Sothoth.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a very good point. If I truly wanted to include Cthulhu Mythos creatures in a more accurate way, they'd be like a mix of Abyssals and Aliens (M:tAw Summoners). However, I would not confirm what they are nor the limits of their powers. Uncertainty is scary to humanity as a whole, and even more so for the Awakened. After all, when you are a metaphorical living library of occult knowledge, but still can't figure out how to fight that <i><b>thing, </b></i>you know shit just got real. Or anti-real, rather.<br /> <br /> But there is another way to use the Cthulhu Mythos for inspiration, although it is not what the OP asked for. You can project your human perspective into those monsters' actions, apply reasoning to them and turn your extrapolations into human or quasi-human personality traits. That is, you end up with PCs that have significant aesthetic resemblance to Great Old Ones/Outer Gods, but aren't. It is admittedly a very big stretch and sort of defeats the purpose. But I like to think of it as changing the purpose with a question: &quot;what if these alien gods and monsters were human?&quot; Human in this case means with a sufficiently human-like mindset, not necessarily appearance.<br /> <br /> Let's try it, shall we? I'll go with the poster boy, but I'll explain my interpretations of the others if enough interest is shown.<br /> <br /> Have you ever watched<b> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-DsgZ4JXXB8&amp;list=PL301FC6482AB0090F\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Calls For Cthulhu&quot;</a></b> or read <b><a href=\"http://www.neilgaiman.com/p/Cool_Stuff/Short_Stories/I_Cthulhu\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I, Cthulhu&quot;</a></b>? If we take cues from these parodies, PC Cthulhu is: abrasive, fatalistic, commanding, usually informal, slow to have strong emotional responses and occasionally allows himself to be merciful and a bit whimsical. In short, he has lots of power and poise, but is still bored and stuck with his &quot;job&quot;. He has a few moments of hope, but he mostly reeks of ancient cynicism. He has to answer to forces even bigger than him, while also administrating the duties of those below him, whom he can't help but see as puny and fleeting. He is more cunning and charismatic than actually intelligent, preferring a &quot;Jack Of All Trades, Master Of None&quot; approach to academia. He stays inactive or nearly inactive for long periods, sending visions to his cultists so they have some notion of what to do. His rising is spoken of in shaking whispers, and in the first moments of his on-screen appearance, he is indeed larger than life. However, he gets placed again into his magic coma by being rammed through the head by a boat. With all of this in mind, I'd say that re-imagining him as a Makara Beast with a Hunger For Ruin is superficial. He works much better as a Mummy. He sends visions through the aptly named &quot;Dreams Of Dead Gods&quot; Utterance. R'lyeh is his Tomb, the Necronomicon is a Relic, his cyclic increase and decrease of power is the usual Arisen deal. The popular fanart he has IRL and in the NWOD is based on the stone idol from his debut story. When he is seen firsthand, he is described as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Call Of Cthulhu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no language for such abysms of shrieking and immemorial lunacy, such eldritch contradictions of all matter, force, and cosmic order. A mountain walked or stumbled. God! What wonder that across the earth a great architect went mad, and poor Wilcox raved with fever in that telepathic instant? The Thing of the idols, the green, sticky spawn of the stars, had awaked to claim his own. The stars were right again, and what an age-old cult had failed to do by design, a band of innocent sailors had done by accident. After vigintillions of years great Cthulhu was loose again, and ravening for delight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The apparent malevolence is in the mortals' eyes, and understandably so. Perhaps Arisen!Cthulhu also used one of his other powers to look scarier than usual so the invaders would just leave his Tomb and let him go about his business. They refused and got an eye-widening, profanity-inducing amount of Successes on a Dexterity + Firearms roll with flamethrowers or something.<br /> <br /> If you really wanna portray him as a Begotten, please remember a few things. He isn't a mustache-twirling destroyer of empires, so Ravager doesn't fit. Makara is only fitting because of the Kraken imagery, but it is his <b>idol</b> that looks Kraken-ish! He and R'lyeh have been described as &quot;cyclopean&quot; many times, and the core fear behind his concept is powerlessness of humanity as a whole. When you look at Cthulhu, you don't think &quot;that monster must know a lot of secrets&quot;, you think &quot;holy shit that thing is HUGE oh God help m--&quot; <b>*gets squished*</b>. His Family should be Anakim. Hunger For Prey and Punishment wouldn't work either for the same reason Ravager doesn't. That leaves us with Hunger For Hoard and Power. Either of those might be interesting, I believe.<br /> <br /> What does everybody think?<br /> <br /> EDIT: if people wanna know more, I'll start another thread so as to not derail this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-01-2015, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T07:29:57-07:00","id":612213,"title":"","content":"This entire thread gives me the urge to do a conversion of the Call of Cthulhu RPG into the WoD mechanics...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:39:14-07:00","id":615567,"title":"","content":"Doing the Lovecraftian Mythos is easy in Changeling. The True Fae can be entire universes or even multiverses with they're own rules/physics alien to the human mind, they can twist Changelings into all kinds of horrid forms, heck, a True Fae could use a single title to create an earth like world, and have beings like Cthululu exist not as direct entities one interacts with, but as kind of twisted laws of physics that mad cultists idolize as beings of utter horror.<br /> <br /> You could have a chronicle of changelings who haven't escaped yet and in fact don't realize they're not really on Earth.<br /> <br /> As unescaped Changelings, they completely vulnerible to the True Fae's power, although they don't know it.<br /> <br /> That should give you all the nilihistic horror you could wish for.<br /> <br /> Now image that True Fae has a second title and uses it to create a Prop verison of the Necromanticon. Props are Insanely powerful and maybe the purpose of this one is make the Mortal World more like the True Fae's realm title, a Lovecraftian World. So the purpose of the prop is merge the mortal world, with the True Fae's Realm.<br /> <br /> There is also an Lovecraftian Horror trapped in the Dreams world by the True Fae.<br /> <br /> I also like the Lovecraftian Horrors in second sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:59:53-07:00","id":615617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=615567#post615567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing the Lovecraftian Mythos is easy in Changeling. The True Fae can be entire universes or even multiverses with they're own rules/physics alien to the human mind, they can twist Changelings into all kinds of horrid forms, heck, a True Fae could use a single title to create an earth like world, and have beings like Cthululu exist not as direct entities one interacts with, but as kind of twisted laws of physics that mad cultists idolize as beings of utter horror.<br /> <br /> You could have a chronicle of changelings who haven't escaped yet and in fact don't realize they're not really on Earth.<br /> <br /> As unescaped Changelings, they completely vulnerible to the True Fae's power, although they don't know it.<br /> <br /> That should give you all the nilihistic horror you could wish for.<br /> <br /> Now image that True Fae has a second title and uses it to create a Prop verison of the Necromanticon. Props are Insanely powerful and maybe the purpose of this one is make the Mortal World more like the True Fae's realm title, a Lovecraftian World. So the purpose of the prop is merge the mortal world, with the True Fae's Realm.<br /> <br /> There is also an Lovecraftian Horror trapped in the Dreams world by the True Fae.<br /> <br /> I also like the Lovecraftian Horrors in second sight.</div> </div> </div> </div> Allow me to point you towards <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/168334-arkham-lost\">a very relevant homebrew</a></b>. Btw, it's called Necronomicon, not Necromanticon. The latter would be a Decepticon who transforms into a grimoire, or a necromancer manticore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:53:28-07:00","id":618999,"title":"","content":"I like your home brew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T10:08:49-07:00","id":619052,"title":"","content":"Hey, someone posted my work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:27:31-07:00","id":619753,"title":"","content":"Or the Necromanticon could be a book about Romance and Necromancy &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Maybe give it to someone like Johann George Faust VIII from Shaman King. A necromancer trying to bring his true love back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 08-08-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:32:33-07:00","id":619756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=619753#post619753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the necromanticon could be a book about Romance and Necromancy &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello. I am a Galateid.<br /> <br /> While I understand the implication and meaning behind the quoted post, could someone please explain why the normal user of this account is pouring bleach in his ears? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-08-2015, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:55:30-07:00","id":619788,"title":"","content":"I'm not, that's just what first came to my mind the moment I read the word Necromanticon cuz the word romantic is right in there &lt;.&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T20:01:10-07:00","id":630584,"title":"","content":"It should be pretty easy, right? All of Lovecraft's monsters were just aliens with superior technology that we couldn't recognize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T20:08:43-07:00","id":630591,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, Deviant could be a pretty good light Lovecraftian game; the ambiguity of your mutators being sorcerers or scientists is right there in the pitch, they could be wizards of Yog-Sothoth and it wouldn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> Neatly ties into the horror of alienation and seeing the dark side of the world. Also makes the cultists the main villains, which is probably what you should be doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:09:09-07:00","id":631839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=630584#post630584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be pretty easy, right? All of Lovecraft's monsters were just aliens with superior technology that we couldn't recognize.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not all of them. You are right in the case of beings like the Mi-Go, Elder Things and Great Race Of Yith. As for Nyarlathotep, the use of weird sciences is just one of his powers, the other two most commonly shown being multiversal travel and near limitless shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> For the most part, Lovecraft's monsters didn't need advanced and wondrous mechanisms built over eons of increasing understanding and artifice. They simply operate on physical principles that are vastly different from the ones we accept as &quot;correct&quot;, often to terrifying and deadly levels.<br /> <br /> While these alien laws of matter, energy and space-time affect our universe in usually harmful ways, the laws of our universe seldom appear to be a major inconvenience to these creatures. Perhaps the only ones that can stay for relatively long periods on our plane of existence without breaking down or being violently expelled are those who possess some kind of mastery or aptitude with imposing their laws over ours.<br /> <br /> There could be some obscure hierarchy/sequencing of realms that determines the difficulty and means of transfer between them. &quot;The stars are right&quot; does not solely refer to the planets in our solar system being aligned. This alignment is merely a key that can only unlock the gateways to eldritch domains from our side. The beings who are interested in coming to our universe for their own alien reasons gather cultists, servants and other allies precisely to facilitate their manifestation.<br /> <br /> It is possible that in a domain with no stars at all, grandiose and eyeless vermin of keen hearing perceive the Call as frequencies of sound that make them ill and irrational. They might even perceive the Call as light, which is as absurd a concept to them as the angles of R'lyeh are to us. A measure of dread and awe might even be a requirement for the Call to traverse the many layers of reality in any meaningful capacity.<br /> <br /> In short, their many powers are usually inherent and instinctual, not external and cerebral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-18-2015, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:35:13-07:00","id":632852,"title":"","content":"Shub-Niggurath could also birth, vomit up, or otherwise mutate a potential Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T21:08:09-07:00","id":633013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=631839#post631839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not all of them. You are right in the case of beings like the Mi-Go, Elder Things and Great Race Of Yith. As for Nyarlathotep, the use of weird sciences is just one of his powers, the other two most commonly shown being multiversal travel and near limitless shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> For the most part, Lovecraft's monsters didn't need advanced and wondrous mechanisms built over eons of increasing understanding and artifice. They simply operate on physical principles that are vastly different from the ones we accept as &quot;correct&quot;, often to terrifying and deadly levels.<br /> <br /> While these alien laws of matter, energy and space-time affect our universe in usually harmful ways, the laws of our universe seldom appear to be a major inconvenience to these creatures. Perhaps the only ones that can stay for relatively long periods on our plane of existence without breaking down or being violently expelled are those who possess some kind of mastery or aptitude with imposing their laws over ours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so, exactly that. Technology that is not currently understood by us which understanding would make us into something other than human. To Lovecraft, to expand our capacity to understand the universe meant discarding what we currently quantify as &quot;humanity&quot; and change our definitions to suit. He really loved playing with definitions and language, and attempted to force the reader to imagine things that weren't really there through the use of his language.<br /> <br /> At the Mountains of Madness is quite clear on this in its entirety. This whole idea that they're not aliens with advanced technology and are instead some other thing did not come until well after (and Derleth tried to inject his own version of faith into it, and even started giving the characters elemental associations) - Lovecraft was writing science fiction <i>as the</i> <i>science of the day understood it</i> (albeit with his own dislike of the Flash Gordon-type stories so common in the period were - he was under the opinion that putting an Earth human into a situation where he must deal with technologically advanced species would be such a &quot;no contest&quot; situation that it made interactions between the two outright laughable, if not impossible), and it must be cast as something else to fit into our modern understanding of physics - but this is a more complex issue than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There could be some obscure hierarchy/sequencing of realms that determines the difficulty and means of transfer between them. &quot;The stars are right&quot; does not solely refer to the planets in our solar system being aligned. This alignment is merely a key that can only unlock the gateways to eldritch domains from our side. The beings who are interested in coming to our universe for their own alien reasons gather cultists, servants and other allies precisely to facilitate their manifestation. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't suddenly make them <i>not </i>aliens with technology we don't understand, and it actually seems to lend more credence to the fact that they are &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is possible that in a domain with no stars at all, grandiose and eyeless vermin of keen hearing perceive the Call as frequencies of sound that make them ill and irrational. They might even perceive the Call as light, which is as absurd a concept to them as the angles of R'lyeh are to us. A measure of dread and awe might even be a requirement for the Call to traverse the many layers of reality in any meaningful capacity. </div> </div> </div>Right, so, multiverse theory. Again, At the Mountains of Madness is quite clear that they're all aliens simply not operating under human constraits given the technological limitations of the 1920s/30s. Lovecraft was very annoyed with science fiction of the day and his works are largely a response to the current zeitgeist of how aliens acted. I mean, really, the entire &quot;universe too big, aliens don't care enough to even give you the bird as they fly off&quot; thing was such a mind-blowing concept that we're still projecting occult/magical phenomena into his works to this day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, their many powers are usually inherent and instinctual, not external and cerebral. </div> </div> </div>Would you call use of a pacemaker external and cerebral? Plastic knee? What about a language system? We could also talk about memetic support infrastructures and how they develop without direct input other than a communication method - you know, are the statements &quot;don't go swimming until 30 minutes after you've eaten&quot; or &quot;MSG is bad for you&quot; external and cerebral given that they are demonstrably incorrect but still embedded in the cultural infrastructure of the Americas? How about entirely iconographic languages that work on object association memory? Most of our technology is inextricably intertwined with our instinctive patterns, and is utilized as a whole without regard for its function or even its purpose. Most technology studies don't even recognize a human as separate from its technology, given that our brain, within thirty minutes, accepts any tool being utilized as a part of its body - smart phones are straight up prosthetic brains that impact people the same way memory loss does when they're removed.The same would be true for a large-scale infrastructure whose purpose was either lost or was supported to maintain one particular entity or more. The difference between Yog-Sothoth and an intelligence computer network designed to monitor transference of field interactions between membranes is practically nil and only possible to be seen as a different when the viewer doesn't even know what a computer network or interacting membranes are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:06:03-07:00","id":633911,"title":"","content":"The thing is, though, that a being like Yog-Sothoth is so fundamentally unlike us that calling it &quot;just an alien with superior technology&quot; is misleading. You're right in that Yoggie can perhaps be compared to a form of technology (being &quot;the key and the gate&quot;), but it can also cause (and perhaps be induced to cause) human women to give birth to giant invisible monsters and not-quite-human things with tentacles coming out of their waist. It's the kind of thing that moves &quot;not in the spaces we know, but between them,&quot; but also the kind of thing which can be summoned, at least in part, into the material space that we're familiar with. Contact with it can be damaging to the rational mind, but it can grant understanding and power and access to strange other realms and distant places. It seems to <i>want</i> things, though this could merely be human beings projecting their own desires and fears onto it. It is, for an intents and purposes, a god, but is inexplicably bound by certain limitations which make it possible to oppose those machinations which at least <i>appear</i> to be its will.<br /> <br /> Although it's not really a distinction that Lovecraft would have used or necessarily agreed with, this is why it can be useful to distinguish Lovecraft's alien gods into two groups, which the Call of Cthulhu RPG calls &quot;Great Old Ones&quot; and &quot;Elder Gods.&quot; Cthulhu is located in a distinct place, apparently likes to have a house to live in, and you can ram a boat into him. Yog-Sothoth was and is and will be, everywhere and nowhere all at once, and you can no more hit him with a boat than you could punch gravity.<br /> <br /> Also, At the Mountains of Madness is, for the most part, about one particular group of starfish-barrel aliens, who are explicitly compared to humans in their goals and the way they order their society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-20-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T05:15:01-07:00","id":1117678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=466898#post466898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh... In my opinion, WoD is too empowering to humanity to play well with the Lovecraft mythos. Lovecraft's stories were all about how small and insignificant humans are in the face of omnipotent uncaring gods from the farthest reaches of the cosmos. In the World of Darkness, every single human has the potential within their soul to become a living symbol that can define and re-define reality any way it sees fit, and artificial beings wielding the divine fire would gladly give up their power to become human... I just don't see them meshing well, at least not without damaging a big part of what makes the Lovecraft mythos so horrifying. That said, there are plenty of godlike alien beings in WoD, so it should theoretically be possible if you aren't married to Lovecraft's themes of existential nihilism. Wouldn't be my choice, but different strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree here. I was recently trying to work on a Beast Chronicle (well, prepare anyways) set in present day Arkham. It's rather difficult to do, for me anyways, because of my love for anything Lovecraft (I have the entire collection of works, letters, etc. all leatherbound in my bookshelf and copies to read...I'm that guy). I scrapped it because I could not achieve the level of horror that <i>is</i> the mythos. Not with Beast anyways. I have seen some adaptations meant for Mortal games in Arkham, but again, I just have a hard time setting the Chronicles of Darkness in Arkham, Dunwich, Innsmouth, etc. without failing the level of horror I feel Lovecraft achieved with his work.<br /> <br /> I figure if I want Lovecraft, I'll crack open Arkham Horror or Eldritch Horror and play a 3-4 hour game (unfortunately 1 player because my wife and children absolutely cannot stand it lol) or quite possibly run through one of the old solo CoC modules (remember those?!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T05:58:24-07:00","id":1117691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology#post466802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast thread, in which I posited Cthulhu as a Makara/Ruin Beast, got me thinking...<br /> <br /> Is it possible to fit the whole Lovecraftian mythos into the framework of the World of Darkness, without changing anything on either end? I'm imagining Nyarlathotep, for example, as as an Arch-Qashmal (Lilithim, obviously.)<br /> <br /> You have any thoughts on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm not overly familiar with Lovecraft, but I will say that the Abyss is filled with Lovecraftian references. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:33:40-07:00","id":1117761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=1117691#post1117691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not overly familiar with Lovecraft, but I will say that the Abyss is filled with Lovecraftian references. </div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is full of Lovecraftian aesthetic. But it's thematically not very Lovecraftian, in my opinion. Actually very, very little modern work adapts Lovecraft's themes well, despite his Asthetics being all over modern horror. <br /> <br /> The thing is, Lovecraft's horror came from the realization that despite all of our science and technology, we don't know shit about how the universe really works. And if we ever found out, our puny brains wouldn't be able to handle it. But that's not a particularly horrifying revelation in this day and age. We have celebrity scientists telling us that science is an ongoing process of trying to explain things the best we can with limited information. We're much more comfortable with the idea of an unknowable universe than most people were in the 20s and 30s.<br /> <br /> Awakening is a thematic inversion of Lovecraft. It's about characters who get a glimpse of how the universe really works, and instead of breaking them, that knowledge empowers them to become super-beings. The Abyss may have the trappings of alien intellect and tentacles and Things That Should Not Be. But in Lovecraft's work, the horror is in the fact that the eldritch beings actually <i>should</i> be and <i>are</i>; it's only because of our limited perspective that we think they shouldn't. In Awakening, the Abyss quite literally should not be. It's not beyond our ability to comprehend because the truth is inherently beyond our grasp, the Abyss is incomprehensible because it's actually literally impossible, and exists anyway as a side effect of your power to define reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-18-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:13:55-07:00","id":1117790,"title":"","content":"I didn't say to use Awakening; Lovecraft really didn't suggest witches and wizards for his main characters, after all. If you want to talk about people who see the underlying bits of the universe and struggle to make sense of it, going a bit insane, then we're going to go with mortals and their Integrity. Integrity is pretty much just a WoD version of Sanity. You can use the Abyss as a threat even in a mortal game. And if you're not comfortable with that much? Then just translate them into Horrors. <br /> <br /> All in all, I think such a conversion is fairly easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:16:19-07:00","id":1117794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> --Regarding your parody portrayal of Cthulu: I find your product and/or service intriguing and wish to subscribe to your newsletter. Do Yog-Sothoth next, perhaps? As CatDoom points out Yogie there is a barrel of contradictions swimming in the space-time superfluid. Or something. <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=1117761#post1117761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss is full of Lovecraftian aesthetic. But it's thematically not very Lovecraftian, in my opinion. Actually very, very little modern work adapts Lovecraft's themes well, despite his Asthetics being all over modern horror.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Lovecraft's horror came from the realization that despite all of our science and technology, we don't know shit about how the universe really works. And if we ever found out, our puny brains wouldn't be able to handle it. But that's not a particularly horrifying revelation in this day and age. We have celebrity scientists telling us that science is an ongoing process of trying to explain things the best we can with limited information. We're much more comfortable with the idea of an unknowable universe than most people were in the 20s and 30s.<br /> <br /> Awakening is a thematic inversion of Lovecraft. It's about characters who get a glimpse of how the universe really works, and instead of breaking them, that knowledge empowers them to become super-beings. The Abyss may have the trappings of alien intellect and tentacles and Things That Should Not Be. But in Lovecraft's work, the horror is in the fact that the eldritch beings actually <i>should</i> be and <i>are</i>; it's only because of our limited perspective that we think they shouldn't. In Awakening, the Abyss quite literally should not be. It's not beyond our ability to comprehend because the truth is inherently beyond our g[r]asp, the Abyss is incomprehensible because it's actually literally impossible, and exists anyway as a side effect of your power to define reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this is true, and it's one of the things that bothered me about the Abyss and what it is and is supposed to represent in the nWoD cosmology. It's just too pat, in a way: the Abyss wasn't, then it was, after the attempt at conquering heaven was partially successful. So... the argument continues as to why, but it's been firmly established for the sake of publishing product that the Abyss constitutes the concept of &quot;untruth&quot; on contrast to Supernal &quot;truth&quot; -- which is in fact subjective truth thanks to the Exarchs meddling with it, not that the Fallen World would know the difference.<br /> <br /> And I think there's some missed opportunities here, at least if what you're aiming for is a game experience of reality horror and not just a colorful trip. Namely, the Abyss could be the things that *should* be and *are* but *are not* because of meddling humans. Only, since they were/are in fact true, and the Exarchs are products of the World and thus dependent on previous truth to substantiate their existence--ever--then Cthulu can't be un-true--his truth has to be &quot;killed&quot; and left dreaming until even the truth of Death may die.<br /> <br /> So, then, the Abyss isn't just want is not true, it is what is true but is being swept aside because it's inconvenient to the foibles of the Exarchs at the time. There are multiple Atlantis-es, but there has to be an Atlantis because something you can label as that was/is foundational to the Exarchs, who are true in their state and past--minds being bound by a relative passage of Time.<br /> <br /> And Yog-Sothoth is true, even if he's not part of present reality &quot;truth&quot;, because he cannot be gotten rid of without removing a necessary support for the Exarch(s). So, when a human mind--even an Awakened human mind--encounters Yog-Sothoth she encounters Truth. <i>Truth that is clearly not supposed to be true, but is so. </i>Yog-Sothoth isn't a lie, the lie is that Yog-Sothoth isn't there, and that lie is the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Does this help? Mage makes me want to scream, so it's hard to tell.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:45:20-07:00","id":1117809,"title":"","content":"If we say that a Lovecraftian horror is things which are and should be, but we can't comprehend them, I think that a good example of such being in Awakening are the Old Gods of the Supernal- you know, those ancient symbols from before humanity which devour souls and were banished by the Exarchs when they Ascent. On the other hand, you may say that Awakening is a very Lovecraftian game from a mortal's point of view- magic breaks the mind of regular people who witness it, as their minds can't comprehend the truth. Humanity lives in a Lie it tells itself since they very beginning of time to make it feel safe and protected. Mages are terrible people who were touched by primordial forces older than mankind, and are now able to invoke unknown horrors using occult symbols. The Watchtowers are not beacon of light in the darkness, but castles of madness which draw those souls and unstable minds of those that can accept the truth, that the world is wider and deeper than what any mortal mind could imagine. The Supernal is not somewhere up in the heavens- it is all around you, lurking, whispering, twisting and coiling. Your limited mind just can't see it, and those who do are driven mad by fear and terror. The Old Ones are already here, called as angels and demons and faeries by those who try to give a name to the nameless and face to the faceless in a poor attempt to understand the vastness of the universe.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say, that maybe we are looking at it all wrong- the world could look quit sane when you look at it from the eyes of a madman, after all... or in other words, what if Cthulhu does not lurk in the Abyss, but sits under the the Watchtower of Iron Gauntlet? What if the Abyss, with all of its horror, is not the power which tries to destroy the world, but humanity's last hope?<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm not a Scelestus I just look like one)</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:51:06-07:00","id":1117813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=1117790#post1117790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't say to use Awakening; Lovecraft really didn't suggest witches and wizards for his main characters, after all. If you want to talk about people who see the underlying bits of the universe and struggle to make sense of it, going a bit insane, then we're going to go with mortals and their Integrity. Integrity is pretty much just a WoD version of Sanity. You can use the Abyss as a threat even in a mortal game. And if you're not comfortable with that much? Then just translate them into Horrors. <br /> <br /> All in all, I think such a conversion is fairly easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This raises another interesting point. I don't think Integrity, or Call of Cthulhu's Sanity for that matter, are a great fit for Lovecraft's themes either.<br /> <br /> Sanity works in CoC because CoC is like the tabletop equivalent of a roguelike. You know when you set out that your character is going to die, and you play to see how far you can get before that happens. Sanity in that system is just another HP track, something to grind your character down on until it runs out and you get to try again with a new character.<br /> <br /> CofD takes a slightly different approach to a similar concept with Integrity, modeling the trauma the protagonists experience from witnessing the existentially horrifying, and gives the characters the opportunity to learn and grow from the experience, even as it negatively impacts their psychology.<br /> <br /> Both are good systems for modeling characters being psychologically scarred by their experiences, but I would argue that neither is thematically appropriate for Lovecraft's brand of &quot;madness&quot;. In Lovecraft's stories, part of the horror (which, again, doesn't play as well to modern audiences as it did to Lovecraft's contemporaries) is the suggestion that maybe the apparent madmen are actually the sane ones, and everyone else is just too deluded to see the world as it truly is. Seeing Cthulu doesn't cause you to spontaneously develop mental disorders. It opens your eyes to the truth that has been right in front of you all along, but you wouldn't allow yourself to see. Actually, this is one place where CofD does fit in well with Lovecraftian themes.<br /> <br /> But I think a game system for modeling Lovecraftian madness would look less like CoC's Sanity or CofD's Integrity, and more like Bloodborne's Insight. As you experience eldritch horrors, your understanding of the true nature of the universe actually increases, but in so doing, your experience of reality becomes further from what you would previously have considered normal. You're not hallucinating, you're just seeing very real things no one else can.<br /> <br /> And now I am tempted to start working on house rules for inverting Integrity into Insight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-18-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:56:19-07:00","id":1117815,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>: I actually very much agree with that interpretation. It's a great way to present Mage as antagonists in a mortal game, and much more in line with Lovecraftian themes if that's what you're going for. I've said before that Supernal entities are the best example of cosmic horror in CofD, and I stand by that statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T12:54:43-07:00","id":1117894,"title":"","content":"My two cents is that mortals and supernaturals alike suffer enough in the World of Darkness without bringing Lovecraft into the equation. Maybe we could just give them a little break, ya know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:38:13-07:00","id":1117911,"title":"","content":"Personally I tend to think the cosmic horror label is a little misleading, I think what Lovecraft was actually working with was often the older idea of the sublime. Cthulhu being unknowable isn't really the problem, it's that they're a walking mountain who can wipe out Humanity at a whim and there's nothing that can be done.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to intellectually accept our comparitive precariousness in the universe, it's another to come face to face with the executioner.<br /> <br /> To add to that, despite the stereotype, a lot of the characters in Lovecraft works don't really go mad. They seem more like people who have been given an arbitrary stay of execution (sometimes literally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:59:56-07:00","id":1118251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/466802-fitting-the-lovecraft-mythology-into-the-world-of-darkness-s-cosmology?p=1117761#post1117761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening is a thematic inversion of Lovecraft. It's about characters who get a glimpse of how the universe really works, and instead of breaking them, that knowledge empowers them to become super-beings. The Abyss may have the trappings of alien intellect and tentacles and Things That Should Not Be. But in Lovecraft's work, the horror is in the fact that the eldritch beings actually <i>should</i> be and <i>are</i>; it's only because of our limited perspective that we think they shouldn't. In Awakening, the Abyss quite literally should not be. It's not beyond our ability to comprehend because the truth is inherently beyond our grasp, the Abyss is incomprehensible because it's actually literally impossible, and exists anyway as a side effect of your power to define reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend John and I talk about this all the time and our little pet theory is the Supernal is just a sub-realm of the Abyss which is connected to mages and everything supernatural about the world the Chronicles of Darkness , from Uratha and the world having a spirit reflection, all the realms besides the material world, every Ephemeral Being and horror to the Templates are the consequences of long past Abyssal Intrusions into a small pocket of sanity floating within the Abyss. In the beginning there was only the Abyss and something in it created a pocket of stability which is a mundane universe but it's been cracking and leaking in weirdness ever since, until one day the reality firmament that separates the Abyss from the world will break like a dam allowing the Abyss to flood in, and all will be the Abyss again.<br /> <br /> It's a solid unified WoD theory, and oh so Lovecraft. By the way about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biblical_cosmology#The_cosmic_ocean\" target=\"_blank\">real life</a>.vs <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Literature/ToReignInHell\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Yes that'd make Mages themselves a type of Abyssal Intruder which is negatively affected by Abyssal Intrusions that don't match their home realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-19-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}